The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'bigquery-public-data': {'libraries_io': ['repositories', 'dependencies', 'projects', 'versions', 'projects_with_repository_fields', 'repository_dependencies', 'tags']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below is a short “map” of the most relevant columns together with the way they will usually be used for this task, followed by ten exploratory / illustrative SQL queries (from trivial to fairly complex).  
Every query is limited to 20 rows so that it can be run quickly while you familiarise yourself with the data.

==================================================
1.  Important columns and their typical usage
==================================================

• `repositories.id` – join key to / filter by a concrete repository.  
• `repositories.name_with_owner` – human‑readable full repository name required in the final list.  
• `repositories.host_type` – GitHub / GitLab / Bitbucket.  
• `repositories.size` – repository size in kB.  Multiply by 1024 to obtain bytes.  
• `repositories.language` – main language of the repository.  
• `repositories.fork_source_name_with_owner` – non‑null if this repo is a fork.  
• `repositories.updated_timestamp` – last time Libraries.io saw an update for the repository.  
• `repository_dependencies.repository_id` – foreign key that links one dependency row to one concrete repository.  
• `repository_dependencies.dependency_project_name` – name of the package depended on (e.g. “flipper”, “unleash”).  
• `repository_dependencies.manifest_platform` – package manager (npm, Maven, NuGet …).  
• `projects.id` – primary key of a project / package (library).  
• `projects.name` – canonical package / artifact name.  
• `projects.platform` – package manager of that project (npm, Maven, …).  
• `projects.language` – language that Libraries.io attributes to that package.

Main conditions you will normally apply  

1. Restrict the dependency rows to the *feature‑toggle libraries list*  
   WHERE LOWER(dependency_project_name) IN (‘unleash’, ‘flipper’, ‘ldclient‑rb’, …)  
   or (slightly safer) a big `IN` list with all canonical names you care about.

2. Join dependency rows to the source repositories  
   ON repository_dependencies.repository_id = repositories.id

3. (Optional) join dependency rows to the package metadata  
   ON repository_dependencies.dependency_project_id = projects.id

4. Add any further filters you like – for example only GitHub, or only repositories updated after 2020‑01‑01, etc.

==================================================
2.  Ten sample queries
==================================================

```sql
-- 1) Description: First glance – 20 raw repositories.
SELECT *
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repositories`
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: List distinct package managers that appear in dependency manifests.
SELECT DISTINCT manifest_platform
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies`
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: All unique dependency names that contain the word “toggle”.
SELECT DISTINCT dependency_project_name
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies`
WHERE  LOWER(dependency_project_name) LIKE '%toggle%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Look at one particular library (“flipper”) – which
--    package managers is it referenced from?
SELECT DISTINCT manifest_platform
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies`
WHERE  LOWER(dependency_project_name) = 'flipper'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Pick a single library (“unleash”) and show the first
--    20 repositories (just ids and names) that depend on it.
SELECT rd.repository_id,
       r.name_with_owner
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` rd
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repositories`           r
       ON r.id = rd.repository_id
WHERE  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) = 'unleash'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Join dependency rows to the *library project* itself
--    to get the package’s own language and platform information.
SELECT rd.dependency_project_name,
       p.platform  AS package_platform,
       p.language  AS package_language,
       COUNT(*)    AS num_referencing_repos
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` rd
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.projects` p
       ON p.id = rd.dependency_project_id
WHERE  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) IN (
       'unleash', 'flipper', 'ldclient-js', 'ldclient-rb')
GROUP  BY 1, 2, 3
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: All GitHub repositories that depend on *any* library from the
--    long feature‑toggle list (partial list shown for brevity).
SELECT DISTINCT r.name_with_owner
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` rd
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repositories`           r
       ON r.id = rd.repository_id
WHERE  LOWER(r.host_type) = 'github'
  AND  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) IN (
        'unleash', 'ldclient-js', 'flipper', 'toggle', 'featuretoggle',
        'ldclient-node', 'feature_toggles', 'django-waffle')
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Same as #7 but display additional repository‑level info and
--    convert size to *bytes*.
SELECT r.name_with_owner,
       r.host_type,
       r.language,
       r.fork_source_name_with_owner,
       r.updated_timestamp,
       (r.size * 1024) AS size_bytes
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` rd
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repositories`           r
       ON r.id = rd.repository_id
WHERE  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) IN (
        'unleash', 'ldclient-js', 'flipper', 'toggle', 'featuretoggle',
        'ldclient-node', 'feature_toggles', 'django-waffle')
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Bring the library metadata into the same result – we now
--    know the repo, the package it uses, the package manager and the package
--    language.
SELECT r.name_with_owner,
       r.host_type,
       (r.size * 1024)                         AS size_bytes,
       r.language                              AS repo_language,
       r.fork_source_name_with_owner,
       r.updated_timestamp,
       rd.dependency_project_name              AS library_artifact,
       p.name                                  AS library_name,
       p.platform                              AS library_platform,
       p.language                              AS library_language
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` rd
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repositories` r
       ON r.id = rd.repository_id
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.projects`     p
       ON p.id = rd.dependency_project_id
WHERE  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) IN (
        'unleash',
        'ldclient-js', 'ldclient-node', 'ldclient-rb',
        'flipper', 'toggle', 'featuretoggle',
        'fflip', 'feature_toggles', 'ember-feature-flags',
        'django-waffle', 'gargoyle', 'bandiera-client')
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Final “template” query that gives exactly the information
--     requested in the task statement for *all* repositories that use *any*
--     of the predefined feature‑toggle libraries.  Remove the LIMIT when
--     you are ready for the full result set.
SELECT
       r.name_with_owner                               AS repository_full_name,
       r.host_type                                     AS host_platform,
       (r.size * 1024)                                 AS size_bytes,
       r.language                                      AS repository_language,
       r.fork_source_name_with_owner                   AS fork_source,
       r.updated_timestamp                             AS repository_last_update,
       rd.dependency_project_name                      AS library_artifact_name,
       p.name                                          AS library_canonical_name,
       p.language                                      AS library_language
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` rd
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repositories`           r
       ON r.id = rd.repository_id
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.projects`               p
       ON p.id = rd.dependency_project_id
WHERE  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) IN (
       -- JavaScript / TypeScript
       'unleash-client', 'ldclient-js', 'ldclient-node', 'ember-feature-flags',
       'feature-toggles', '@paralleldrive/react-feature-toggles',
       'flipit', 'fflip', 'bandiera-client', '@flopflip/react-redux',
       '@flopflip/react-broadcast',
       -- Java / Kotlin / Scala
       'no.finn.unleash:unleash-client-java', 'org.togglz:togglz-core',
       'org.ff4j:ff4j-core', 'com.launchdarkly:launchdarkly-client',
       'cc.soham:toggle', 'com.tacitknowledge.flip:core',
       -- Go
       'github.com/launchdarkly/go-client',
       'github.com/xchapter7x/toggle',
       'github.com/vsco/dcdr',
       'github.com/unleash/unleash-client-go',
       -- .NET (NuGet)
       'unleash.client', 'launchdarkly.client', 'nfeature',
       'featuretoggle', 'featureswitcher', 'toggler',
       -- Python
       'unleashclient', 'ldclient-py', 'flask-featureflags',
       'gutter', 'feature_ramp', 'flagon', 'django-waffle',
       'gargoyle', 'gargoyle-yplan',
       -- Ruby
       'unleash', 'ldclient-rb', 'rollout', 'feature_flipper',
       'flip', 'setler', 'bandiera-client', 'feature', 'flipper',
       -- PHP
       'launchdarkly/launchdarkly-php', 'dzunke/feature-flags-bundle',
       'opensoft/rollout', 'npg/bandiera-client-php',
       -- iOS (CocoaPods / Carthage)
       'launchdarkly', 'launchdarkly/ios-client'
)
LIMIT 20;
```

You can now adapt and extend query #10 (for example remove the LIMIT, add `ORDER BY r.updated_timestamp DESC`, or restrict to a certain language or hosting service) to obtain the full production answer required.
